meta:
  origin:
    producer: Velasco
    title: LGBTI National Policy Dataset
    description: |-
      The LGBTI National Policy Dataset (Version 2.1) is a country-year-policy panel tracking the adoption, scope, and enforcement of LGBTI-related policies across 195 countries from 1991 to 2025. The dataset is distributed in long format: each row records one country in one year for one specific policy-status combination. It is designed for use in comparative political research, policy diffusion analysis, and quantitative cross-national studies of LGBTI rights.

      The dataset covers 27 distinct policy areas organized into 54 policy-status combinations (each policy paired with two mutually exclusive status directions). Of these 54 combinations, 37 contain substantive data; the remaining 17 are structural placeholders with all-zero values, included to maintain a fully balanced panel suitable for econometric methods.
    citation_full: |-
      Velasco, Kristopher. 2026. "LGBTI National Policy Dataset, Version 2.1." https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/WTA9P.
    attribution_short: Velasco
    version_producer: '2.1'
    url_main: https://osf.io/wta9p/overview
    # Stable OSF link for LGBTI_Policy_Data_Long.csv. NOTE: the file's short GUID (formerly zpd78) was
    # lost when the producer deleted and re-uploaded the file in the 2026-07-24 (v2.1) revision, so this
    # points at the current file resource id — re-derive it from the OSF API if it 404s on a future update.
    url_download: https://osf.io/download/6a636ff7f73288faf9a326b3/
    date_accessed: '2026-07-24'
    # NOTE: The producer revises Version 2.x in place on OSF without a changelog. The 2026-07-24 revision
    # (labeled "Version 2.1" in the LICENSE file the producer added) replaced both data files and the
    # codebook, following coding questions we raised on the June release — compare OSF file dates/hashes
    # when updating, since the version_producer field alone can't distinguish in-place revisions.
    date_published: '2026-07-24'
    # The producer added a LICENSE file (CC BY 4.0) in the 2026-07-24 revision, replacing the earlier
    # no-declared-license state.
    license:
      name: CC BY 4.0
      url: https://osf.io/wta9p/
